    <footnotes>
        <footnote id="F1">Daewoong Co., Ltd. (&quot;DWC&quot;) owns approximately 52% of the outstanding shares of Daewoong Pharmaceutical Co., Ltd. (&quot;DWP&quot;), a company organized under the laws of the Republic of Korea, and may be deemed to have voting and dispositive power over, and to beneficially own, the securities of the Issuer held directly by DWP. The securities reported herein are held directly by DWP and are reported by DWC as indirectly beneficially owned, consistent with the Form 3 filed by DWC with respect to the Issuer on January 29, 2026. DWC disclaims beneficial ownership of such securities except to the extent of its pecuniary interest therein, and the filing of this statement shall not be deemed an admission that DWC is the beneficial owner of such securities for purposes of Section 16 of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934, as amended, or for any other purpose.</footnote>
        <footnote id="F2">On October 30, 2026 (the &quot;Exercise Date&quot;), DWP exercised in full, on a cashless basis pursuant to Section 10 of the Pre-Funded Warrant, Pre-Funded Warrants to purchase 11,236,631 shares of Class A Common Stock at an exercise price of $0.0001 per share. No cash was paid by DWP in connection with the exercise.</footnote>
        <footnote id="F3">Represents 3,822 shares of Class A Common Stock withheld by the Issuer in satisfaction of the aggregate exercise price of the Pre-Funded Warrants in accordance with the net exercise formula set forth in the Pre-Funded Warrant, based on the closing sale price of $0.294 per share on October 29, 2026, the trading day immediately preceding the Exercise Date. As a result of the cashless exercise, 11,232,809 shares of Class A Common Stock were issued to DWP.</footnote>
        <footnote id="F4">The Pre-Funded Warrants were exercisable at any time on or after January 21, 2026 and did not expire until exercised in full. Following the exercise described in footnotes (2) and (3), no Pre-Funded Warrants remain outstanding.</footnote>
        <footnote id="F5">The Common Stock Warrant has an exercise price of $1.09392 per share and is exercisable on or after the Initial Exercise Date and expires at 5:00 p.m. (New York City time) on the Termination Date, as such terms are defined in the form of warrant filed as Exhibit 4.2 to the Issuer's Current Report on Form 8-K filed with the Securities and Exchange Commission on November 12, 2025. The Common Stock Warrant may not be exercised to the extent that, after giving effect to such exercise, the holder together with its affiliates would beneficially own in excess of 49.99% of the Issuer's outstanding Class A Common Stock.</footnote>
        <footnote id="F6">The Senior Secured Convertible Note in the principal amount of $1,500,000 automatically converts, upon the completion by the Issuer of a bona fide third-party financing with aggregate gross cash proceeds of at least $30.0 million (a &quot;Qualified Financing&quot;), into a number of shares of Class A Common Stock (or pre-funded warrants in lieu thereof) equal to 1.3 multiplied by the quotient of (a) the principal amount and accrued but unpaid interest being converted divided by (b) the per share price in the Qualified Financing. The number of shares issuable upon conversion is therefore not determinable at this time.</footnote>
    </footnotes>

